msgstr "ex:record gmeow:expectedText \"source-value\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "expected statement"
msgstr "énoncé attendu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An expected observation statement represented as a native RDF 1.2 triple term, shared with an explicit rdf:reifies binding. Quotation preserves structure without asserting the quoted proposition or implementing a checker."
msgstr "Énoncé d’observation attendu représenté par un terme de triplet RDF 1.2 natif, partagé avec un lien rdf:reifies explicite. La citation conserve la structure sans affirmer la proposition ni implémenter un contrôle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source explicitly supplies this relation and its context."
msgstr "Utiliser lorsque la source fournit explicitement cette relation et son contexte."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inventing missing source bindings or inferring execution and success from this record alone."
msgstr "Éviter d’inventer des liens source absents ou de déduire exécution et réussite de ce seul enregistrement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain actual source values, identities and attribution; preserve supplied wording, language and direction."
msgstr "Conserver valeurs, identités et attribution réelles de la source ; préserver formulation, langue et direction fournies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Source evidence and configuration remain distinct. Competing attributed records may coexist without a preferred claim."
msgstr "Les preuves source et la configuration restent distinctes. Des enregistrements attribués concurrents peuvent coexister sans déclaration privilégiée."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedStatement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Retain the expected triple term and its explicit reification: ex:descriptor gmeow:expectedStatement <<( ex:item gmeow:displayable true )>> ; rdf:reifies <<( ex:item gmeow:displayable true )>> ."
msgstr "Conserver le terme de triplet attendu et sa réification explicite : ex:descriptor gmeow:expectedStatement <<( ex:item gmeow:displayable true )>> ; rdf:reifies <<( ex:item gmeow:displayable true )>> ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedWorldObject|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "expected world object"
msgstr "objet de monde attendu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedWorldObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exact unresolved simulated-object identifier supplied by the source. Resolution requires a provider-and-world-scoped WorldObjectRecord; matching text alone never creates an object identity."
msgstr "Identifiant exact non résolu d’objet simulé fourni par la source. Sa résolution exige un WorldObjectRecord situé dans un fournisseur et un monde ; une égalité textuelle seule ne crée aucune identité d’objet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/expectedWorldObject|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source explicitly supplies this relation and its context."
msgstr "Utiliser lorsque la source fournit explicitement cette relation et son contexte."

